  {
    "id": "D",
    "name": "Corollary 1: The delay crossover",
    "label": "cor:crossover",
    "eqs": "(13), (14)",
    "contract": "Let $\\tau\\ge0$ and $s=t-\\tau$. Every agent has $\\mathcal F(s)$ and no post-$s$ measurements. The optimal common action is $u_i^D=e^{-\\lambda\\tau}(a/v)\\bar Y(s)$ and\n\\[\nJ_D(\\tau)=a-\\frac{a^2}{v}e^{-2\\lambda\\tau}.\n\\]\nThen $J_L<J_D(\\tau)$ exactly when $\\tau>(2\\lambda)^{-1}\\log(d/v)$, with equality at that age.",
    "source_start": 155,
    "source_end": 170,
    "steps": [
      {
        "id": "D.1",
        "parent": "D",
        "goal": "G-D",
        "statement": "The Markov property and Proposition 1 give $\\E[X(t)\\mid\\mathcal F(s)]=e^{-\\lambda\\tau}(a/v)\\bar Y(s)$.",
        "source_id": "SRC-014",
        "source_lines": [
          168,
          169
        ],
        "kind": "NORMALIZED",
        "support": "EXPLICIT",
        "deps": [
          "A-G",
          "P",
          "B-OU",
          "B-CE"
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "D.2",
        "parent": "D",
        "goal": "G-D",
        "statement": "Taking this common mean minimizes tracking loss and yields zero disagreement, hence minimizes the team loss.",
        "source_id": "SRC-015",
        "source_lines": [
          169,
          169
        ],
        "kind": "NORMALIZED",
        "support": "EXPLICIT",
        "deps": [
          "D.1",
          "D-loss",
          "B-CE"
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "D.3",
        "parent": "D",
        "goal": "G-D",
        "statement": "The error variance is the displayed $J_D(\\tau)$.",
        "source_id": "SRC-016",
        "source_lines": [
          169,
          169
        ],
        "kind": "NORMALIZED",
        "support": "EXPLICIT",
        "deps": [
          "D.1",
          "D.2",
          "D-vd"
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "D.4",
        "parent": "D",
        "goal": "G-D",
        "statement": "Comparison with $J_L$ yields $J_L<J_D$ if and only if $e^{-2\\lambda\\tau}<v/d$.",
        "source_id": "SRC-017",
        "source_lines": [
          169,
          169
        ],
        "kind": "NORMALIZED",
        "support": "EXPLICIT",
        "deps": [
          "D.3",
          "P"
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "D.5",
        "parent": "D",
        "goal": "G-D",
        "statement": "Taking logarithms gives the exact threshold (14), including its equality case.",
        "source_id": "SRC-018",
        "source_lines": [
          169,
          170
        ],
        "kind": "NORMALIZED",
        "support": "EXPLICIT",
        "deps": [
          "D.4",
          "A-G"
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "D.6",
        "parent": "D",
        "goal": "G-D",
        "statement": "Q.E.D.",
        "source_id": "SRC-018",
        "source_lines": [
          169,
          170
        ],
        "kind": "STRUCTURAL",
        "support": "IMPLICIT",
        "deps": [
          "D.1",
          "D.2",
          "D.3",
          "D.5"
        ]
      }
    ]
