  {
    "id": "H",
    "name": "Theorem 1: Hybrid policy and exponential value",
    "label": "thm:hybrid",
    "eqs": "(15)--(21)",
    "contract": "Under (1)--(4), put $\\rho=e^{-\\lambda\\tau}$ and $s=t-\\tau$. The unique optimal hybrid action is\n\\[\nu_i^H=\\rho\\frac av\\bar Y(s)+\\frac ad[Y_i(t)-\\rho Y_i(s)].\n\\]\nIt also attains the optimum with the larger information $\\mathcal F(s)\\vee\\mathcal F_i(t)$. Its posterior variance and team loss satisfy\n\\[\nP_H=\\rho^2P_n+(1-\\rho^2)P_1,\\qquad\nJ_H=\\rho^2J_P+(1-\\rho^2)J_L,\n\\]\nand $J_L-J_H=\\Delta e^{-2\\lambda\\tau}$.",
    "source_start": 175,
    "source_end": 214,
    "steps": [
      {
        "id": "H.1",
        "parent": "H",
        "goal": "G-H",
        "statement": "CASE $\\tau=0$. The formula is the pooled policy.",
        "source_id": "SRC-019",
        "source_lines": [
          192,
          192
        ],
        "kind": "STRUCTURAL",
        "support": "EXPLICIT",
        "deps": [
          "P"
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "H.2",
        "parent": "H",
        "goal": "G-H",
        "statement": "CASE $\\tau>0$. Prove the remaining claims under this assumption.",
        "source_id": "SRC-020",
        "source_lines": [
