  {
    "id": "R",
    "name": "Theorem 2: Optimal refresh period",
    "label": "thm:refresh",
    "eqs": "(28)--(33)",
    "contract": "Assume fixed finite latency $\\delta\\ge0$, an exact joint pooled-vector refresh with price $c>0$, and locally finite schedules independent of all signal and disturbance processes. Let $\\gamma_m=2\\lambda_m$, $A_m=w_m\\Delta_m e^{-\\gamma_m\\delta}>0$,\n\\[\nB(T)=\\sum_m\\frac{A_m}{\\gamma_m}(1-e^{-\\gamma_mT}),\\qquad\nc_{\\rm crit}=\\sum_mA_m/\\gamma_m.\n\\]\nFor $c\\ge c_{\\rm crit}$, no refreshing minimizes the limiting upper average cost at $J_L^{\\rm tot}$. For $0<c<c_{\\rm crit}$, a periodic schedule is optimal among all admissible schedules. Its unique period solves $B(T^*)-T^*B'(T^*)=c$, and its cost is $J_L^{\\rm tot}-\\sum_m A_m e^{-\\gamma_mT^*}$.",
    "source_start": 284,
    "source_end": 311,
    "steps": [
      {
        "id": "R.1",
        "parent": "R",
        "goal": "G-R",
        "statement": "Define $V_\\delta(T)=B^{\\prime}(T)=\\sum_m A_m e^{-\\gamma_mT}$.",
        "source_id": "SRC-051",
        "source_lines": [
          300,
          300
        ],
        "kind": "NORMALIZED",
        "support": "EXPLICIT",
        "deps": [
          "A-R",
          "D-refresh"
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "R.2",
        "parent": "R",
        "goal": "G-R",
        "statement": "Differentiate (29): $C^{\\prime}(T)=[H(T)-c]/T^2$, where $H(T)=B(T)-TV_\\delta(T)$.",
        "source_id": "SRC-052",
        "source_lines": [
          300,
          304
        ],
        "kind": "NORMALIZED",
        "support": "EXPLICIT",
        "deps": [
          "R.1",
          "D-refresh",
          "B-calc"
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "R.3",
        "parent": "R",
        "goal": "G-R",
        "statement": "$H^{\\prime}(T)=-TV_\\delta^{\\prime}(T)>0$ for $T>0$, and $H$ increases from zero to $c_{\\rm crit}$.",
        "source_id": "SRC-053",
        "source_lines": [
          304,
          304
        ],
        "kind": "NORMALIZED",
        "support": "EXPLICIT",
        "deps": [
          "R.1",
          "R.2",
          "A-R",
          "B-calc"
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "R.4",
        "parent": "R",
        "goal": "G-R",
        "statement": "ASSUME $0<c<c_{\\rm crit}$. PROVE a unique minimizing positive period and its displayed value.",
        "source_id": "SRC-054",
        "source_lines": [
          304,
          304
        ],
        "kind": "STRUCTURAL",
        "support": "EXPLICIT",
        "deps": [
          "A-R"
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "R.4.1",
        "parent": "R.4",
        "goal": "R.4",
        "statement": "There is a unique root $H(T^*)=c$, and $C$ decreases before it and increases after it.",
        "source_id": "SRC-054",
        "source_lines": [
          304,
          304
        ],
        "kind": "NORMALIZED",
        "support": "EXPLICIT",
        "deps": [
          "R.2",
          "R.3",
          "B-calc"
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "R.4.2",
        "parent": "R.4",
        "goal": "R.4",
        "statement": "$C(T)\\to\\infty$ as $T\\downarrow0$ and $C(T)\\to J_L^{\\rm tot}$ as $T\\to\\infty$, proving the unique global periodic minimum.",
        "source_id": "SRC-055",
        "source_lines": [
          304,
          304
        ],
        "kind": "NORMALIZED",
        "support": "EXPLICIT",
        "deps": [
          "R.4.1",
          "D-refresh",
